WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.480
- [Instructor] In this
video we're going to get

00:00:01.480 --> 00:00:05.100
a little bit of practice
divided by a two digit number.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.670
So let's say that we have 4,781

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:14.150
divided by 32.

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:16.090
Pause this video and see
if you can figure out

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:17.020
what that's going to be.

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:17.970
And if there is a remainder,

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:20.420
figure out what that
remainder is going to be.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:22.460
All right, now let's
work on this together.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:27.460
So first let me rewrite 4,781

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:32.960
and this is going to be divided by 32.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:35.110
Now whenever we divide by anything

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:36.420
that has more than one digit,

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:37.670
so it's a little bit of an art.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.180
The way we're going to tackle it is

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:42.610
a little trial and error using estimation.

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:44.457
So we'll start by saying "Hey,

00:00:44.457 --> 00:00:46.860
"how many times does 32 go into four?"

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:49.860
Well, 32 doesn't go into four
at all, so then we'll move on.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:54.200
How many times does 32 go into 47?

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:58.840
Well it's pretty clear that
32 goes one time into 47.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:02.890
So I'll put the one right over
there, above the seven in 47.

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:04.850
And if you're saying, "Hey,
how did Sal know that?"

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:07.400
Well, just remember, two
times 32 would be 64.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.110
That's more than 47.

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:14.110
So 32 goes into 47 one time,
and we multiply one times 32.

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:17.210
One times two is two,
one times three is three.

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:19.720
You know that one times 32 is 32.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:23.250
And then we subtract 32 from 47.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:26.170
Let's do that, and we get

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:28.890
seven minus two is five

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:31.700
and four minus three is one.

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:34.280
And the way you make sure
that you did that step right

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:38.210
is whatever we get over
here should be less than 32.

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:40.170
If whatever we have here is 32 or greater,

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:43.010
that means we could of had
a larger number up here.

00:01:43.010 --> 00:01:47.260
But then our next step is
we bring down the eight

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:51.940
and we say, "How many
times does 32 go into 158?"

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:52.970
Now this is a little bit tricky.

00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:54.670
If you were estimating how many times

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:58.610
does 30 go into 150,

00:01:58.610 --> 00:01:59.610
you might say five.

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:01.820
And actually this is for
kicks, let's just try that out.

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:03.640
Let's see if five works.

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:07.830
So let's see, five times two is 10.

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:09.620
We'll put zero ones and then

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:12.250
we will have one 10 there, carry the one.

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:15.730
Fives times three is 15, plus one is 16.

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:16.960
So that didn't work out.

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:19.210
It almost worked out, but not quite.

00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:23.320
160 is larger 158 so
five is too much there.

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:27.960
So we need to go down to four.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:30.480
So four times two is eight.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:33.340
Four times three is 12.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:38.073
And now we subtract and 158 minus 128,

00:02:38.073 --> 00:02:40.190
eight mins eight is zero,

00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:42.500
five tens minus two tens is three tens,

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:43.650
and then we have no hundreds.

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:46.640
And then this is right,
'cause 30 is less than 32.

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:49.320
And then we can bring down,

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:51.800
we can bring down that one.

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:55.060
Now how many times does 32 go into 301?

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:56.157
Well we might be tempted to say,

00:02:56.157 --> 00:02:57.287
"Well, this is close to 30,

00:02:57.287 --> 00:03:00.000
"this is close to 300, so maybe it's 10."

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.680
But 10 times 32 would be
320, so that'd be too much.

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:07.340
So I feel good about nine as my estimate.

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:11.190
Nine times two is 18, carry the one.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:16.130
Nine times three is 27, plus one is 28.

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:18.650
And then we can subtract.

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:20.860
We're actually going to have
to do a little regrouping here.

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:22.350
You might be able to do it in your head.

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:24.970
To go from 288 to 301, let's see,

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:28.080
you would add 12 to get to
300 and then one more, 13.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:29.620
So you might be able to do it in your head

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:32.180
that this is going to be
13, or you could regroup.

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:33.247
You could say, "All right, let's see,

00:03:33.247 --> 00:03:36.047
"one is less than eight, can
I regroup from the 10s place?

00:03:36.047 --> 00:03:37.337
"No, I have nothing there
so I have to regroup

00:03:37.337 --> 00:03:38.817
"from the hundreds place.

00:03:38.817 --> 00:03:40.257
"So I'm gonna take one of those hundreds,

00:03:40.257 --> 00:03:41.467
"I'm left with two hundreds left.

00:03:41.467 --> 00:03:43.187
"And then I'm going to have 10 10s.

00:03:43.187 --> 00:03:44.777
"And then I could take one of those 10s,

00:03:44.777 --> 00:03:47.157
"so I have nine 10s left,
and give it to the ones place

00:03:47.157 --> 00:03:48.687
"so now I have 11 ones.

00:03:48.687 --> 00:03:52.307
"And 11 minus eight is 3,
nine 10s minus eight 10s

00:03:52.307 --> 00:03:54.377
"is one 10, and then hundreds,

00:03:54.377 --> 00:03:56.700
"200 minus 200 is just a zero."

00:03:56.700 --> 00:04:00.210
And so there we have it,
this is less than 32.

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:02.160
We have nothing left to bring down

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:05.300
and so we're left with
the remainder of 13.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:08.210
So this is going to be equal to 149

00:04:08.210 --> 00:04:11.993
with a remainder of 13, and we're done.

